-- check/bad (project): §10.1's two-span case. `Shape` has no `draw`, and the
-- call that made `a` concrete is HERE — so the primary span is
-- `Lib.render shape` at 11:5 in this file, and the callee's `where` clause is
-- named in the prose. Roc reports the callee's span instead and report 18
-- §2.4 is the complaint about it; report 20 §7.2 confirms Roc still does.
import Lib


pub type Shape
    = Circle Float


pub show : Shape -> String
show shape =
    Lib.render shape
